;; Workspace-root clj-kondo config.
;;
;; Each lab has its own .clj-kondo/config.edn, which is what `bb check:lint`
;; picks up because it runs with that lab as the working directory. Editors,
;; though, are usually rooted at this repository, so they resolve THIS config
;; dir instead and never see the per-lab one. Without the entries below,
;; macro-defined vars show up as "Unresolved symbol" in the Problems panel
;; while the command line stays clean — the same rule, two different answers.
;;
;; So this file mirrors the per-lab :lint-as entries. Adding one to a lab means
;; adding it here too, or the editor and CI will disagree again.
;;
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; :exclude-files is the same disagreement, one level up.
;;
;; This repository is not one project. It is forty-odd independent ones, each
;; with its own root, deps.edn and toolchain, and a namespace only resolves
;; relative to the project that owns it. Linting them all from here reports
;; things that are not true: `registry.server/build-router is called with 0
;; args but expects 3` about a function that takes none, and `Unresolved var:
;; post-json` about a var defined nine lines above the use. Both vanish when
;; the same files are linted from their own roots, which is how `bb lint`
;; runs them.
;;
;; So the editor is told to skip the two trees it cannot reason about:
;;
;;   archive/              earlier full-stack projects, each with its own root.
;;                         Kept for reference and outside the lab sequence, and
;;                         provably clean when linted where they live.
;;   .clj-kondo/imports/   config exported by a library. Not ours, and not
;;                         fixable by us.
;;
;; The labs themselves are deliberately not excluded. A finding in lab0..lab34
;; is a real finding and should stay loud — a Problems panel that is always
;; red is one nobody reads.
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Unanchored on purpose: clj-kondo reports `./archive/...` when linting `.`
;; and `archive/...` when given the path directly, so a `^` anchor matches one
;; invocation and silently not the other. Neither string occurs anywhere else
;; in the tree.
{:output {:exclude-files ["archive/" "\\.clj-kondo/imports/"]}
 :lint-as {;; 04b-event-store: defspec defines a var named by its first argument.
           clojure.test.check.clojure-test/defspec clojure.test/deftest

           ;; 03-task-persistence: both return a reified protocol instance.
           spy.protocol/mock clojure.core/reify
           spy.protocol/spy  clojure.core/reify

           ;; lab26: binds a name to the new context and evaluates a body.
           steffan-westcott.clj-otel.api.trace.span/with-span-binding clojure.core/let}}
